module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Koszul.Sheaf.Contraction
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# The Koszul differential on the sectionwise exterior algebra of a presheaf of modules

Let `O` be a presheaf of commutative rings on a category `C`, let `F` be a presheaf of
`O`-modules and let `φ : F → O` be a map of presheaves of modules. Stacks tag 062K attaches to
`φ` the *Koszul complex* `K_•(φ)`: the graded algebra `⋀(F)` together with the unique derivation
whose value on a local section `e` of `F = K₁(φ)` is `φ(e)`.

The graded algebra is
`PresheafOfModules.exteriorAlgebraGradedAlgebra` of
`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.SectionwiseExteriorSymmetricAlgebra`, whose
degree-`n` piece is the presheaf `U ↦ ⋀^n_{O(U)}(F(U))` of sectionwise exterior powers. This
file builds the differential on it: the morphism of presheaves of modules which on sections over
`U` is contraction of `⋀_{O(U)}(F(U))` by the functional `φ_U`.

## Main definitions

* `PresheafOfModules.ExteriorFunctional`: a functional on a presheaf of modules, i.e. a
  sectionwise `O(U)`-linear map `F(U) → O(U)` compatible with restriction. This is the datum
  `φ : F → O` of the source, in the form the sectionwise exterior algebra consumes.
* `PresheafOfModules.exteriorKoszulD`: **the Koszul differential**, a morphism of presheaves of
  modules from the exterior power of degree `n + 1` to the one of degree `n`.

## Main results

* `PresheafOfModules.exteriorAlgebraPieceVal_exteriorKoszulD`: on local sections the
  differential is contraction. Every statement below is deduced from this one together with the
  corresponding ring-level statement, and so is every statement a consumer will need: the
  presheaf of modules `exteriorAlgebraPiece n F` is a submodule of the exterior algebra of the
  sections, and `exteriorAlgebraPieceVal_injective` turns an identity between sections into one
  in that algebra.
* `PresheafOfModules.exteriorKoszulD_comp_exteriorKoszulD`: the differential squares to zero.
* `PresheafOfModules.exteriorAlgebraPieceVal_exteriorKoszulD_gen`: **the defining equation of
  the Koszul differential**, `d e = φ(e)`, on a degree-one generator.
* `PresheafOfModules.exteriorAlgebraPieceVal_exteriorKoszulD_gen_mul`: **the graded Leibniz
  rule**, `d (e ∧ x) = φ(e) · x - e ∧ d x`, on a product whose left factor is a degree-one
  generator. Since the exterior algebra of the sections is generated by `F(U)` over `O(U)`, this
  determines the differential on sections over `U`.
* `PresheafOfModules.exteriorKoszulD_eq_zero_of_neg`: the differential vanishes into a negative
  degree, where the sectionwise exterior algebra has no nonzero sections.

## Implementation notes

**The functional is bundled as `ExteriorFunctional` rather than as a morphism `F ⟶ unit O`.**
The two carry the same information, but a value of `PresheafOfModules.unit O` over `U` is the
ring `O(U)` only after unfolding `unit`, and instance search does not unfold it, so a scalar
action on it is not found; this is the difficulty recorded in the implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras`. The field
`dual` is a `Module.Dual` over the ring of sections, which is the form
`Koszul.contraction` consumes.

**The Leibniz rule is stated with the product as a separate argument.** The product of a
degree-one section and a degree-`n` section has degree `1 + n`, while the differential into
degree `n` has source the piece of degree `n + 1`; those two integers are equal but not
syntactically so, and writing the rule directly therefore needs a transport along
`add_comm`. Instead the rule takes a section `z` of degree `n + 1` together with the hypothesis
that its value is the product, which says the same thing with no transport. This is the idiom of
`SheafOfModules.TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras.tensorPieceZeroIsoUnit_smul_one`.

**Uniqueness of the differential is not proved here, and is not provable at this generality.**
The ring-level statement
`Koszul.HomologicalDifferentialGradedExteriorAlgebra.differential_unique` is proved by
`CliffordAlgebra.left_induction`, which applies because an element of `⋀_{O(U)}(F(U))` is built
from scalars, sums and left multiplication by a generator. That induction is available here as
well, over each `U` separately: it is exactly what makes the Leibniz rule above determine the
differential on `⋀_{O(U)}(F(U))`, so the differential constructed here is the only one. What is
*not* available is the same statement for the degreewise sheafification of this graded algebra,
whose sections over `U` are only locally of that form; see the implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.TensorExteriorSymmetricConstruction`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 062K](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/062K)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0622](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0622)
* [Stacks Project, Section 17.21](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CF)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory Opposite

open scoped ExteriorAlgebra

universe v u w a

namespace PresheafOfModules

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {O : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ CommRingCat.{w}}

/-- **A functional on a presheaf of modules.** It is a linear form on the sections over every
object, compatible with the restriction maps; this is the datum `φ : F → O` of Stacks tag 062K
read sectionwise. -/
structure ExteriorFunctional (F : PresheafOfModules.{max w a} (O ⋙ forget₂ _ RingCat)) where
  /-- The linear form on the sections over an object. -/
  dual (X : Cᵒᵖ) : Module.Dual ((O ⋙ forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat).obj X) (F.obj X)
  /-- The linear forms are compatible with restriction. -/
  naturality {X Y : Cᵒᵖ} (f : X ⟶ Y) (m : F.obj X) :
    ((O ⋙ forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat).map f).hom (dual X m) = dual Y (F.map f m)

variable (F : PresheafOfModules.{max w a} (O ⋙ forget₂ _ RingCat))

/-- **The Koszul differential of a functional on a presheaf of modules.** On sections over `X`
it is contraction of the exterior algebra of `F.obj X` by the linear form `φ.dual X`, which
carries the exterior power of degree `n + 1` into the one of degree `n`. -/
@[sga "7 XII 1.3.1" "more general"]
noncomputable def exteriorKoszulD (φ : ExteriorFunctional.{v, u, w, a} F) (n : ℤ) :
    exteriorAlgebraPiece (n + 1) F ⟶ exteriorAlgebraPiece n F where
  app X := ModuleCat.ofHom (Koszul.intPowD (φ.dual X) n)
  naturality f := ModuleCat.hom_ext (LinearMap.ext fun _x => Subtype.ext
    (Koszul.mapₛₗ_contraction _ (F.restrictₛₗ f) (φ.dual _) (φ.dual _)
      (fun e => φ.naturality f e) _).symm)

variable (φ : ExteriorFunctional.{v, u, w, a} F)

/-- **On local sections the Koszul differential is contraction.** This is the characterization
the rest of the API is deduced from. -/
@[simp]
theorem exteriorAlgebraPieceVal_exteriorKoszulD (n : ℤ) (X : Cᵒᵖ)
    (x : (exteriorAlgebraPiece (n + 1) F).obj X) :
    exteriorAlgebraPieceVal n F X (Hom.app (exteriorKoszulD F φ n) X x) =
      Koszul.contraction (φ.dual X) (exteriorAlgebraPieceVal (n + 1) F X x) :=
  rfl

/-- **The Koszul differential squares to zero.** -/
theorem exteriorKoszulD_comp_exteriorKoszulD (n : ℤ) :
    exteriorKoszulD F φ (n + 1) ≫ exteriorKoszulD F φ n = 0 := by
  refine hom_ext fun X => ModuleCat.hom_ext (LinearMap.ext fun x => ?_)
  refine exteriorAlgebraPieceVal_injective n F X ?_
  rw [exteriorAlgebraPieceVal]
  exact CliffordAlgebra.contractLeft_contractLeft (φ.dual X)
    (exteriorAlgebraPieceVal (n + 1 + 1) F X x)

/-- **The defining equation of the Koszul differential.** Its value on a degree-one generator
`e` is the scalar `φ(e)`, which is Stacks tag 062K's requirement that `d e = φ(e)` for every
local section `e` of `F = K₁(φ)`. -/
theorem exteriorAlgebraPieceVal_exteriorKoszulD_gen (X : Cᵒᵖ) (m : F.obj X) :
    exteriorAlgebraPieceVal 0 F X
        (Hom.app (exteriorKoszulD F φ 0) X (Hom.app (exteriorAlgebraGen F) X m)) =
      algebraMap ((O ⋙ forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat).obj X)
        (ExteriorAlgebra ((O ⋙ forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat).obj X) (F.obj X)) (φ.dual X m) := by
  rw [exteriorAlgebraPieceVal_exteriorKoszulD, exteriorAlgebraPieceVal_gen]
  exact CliffordAlgebra.contractLeft_ι (0 : QuadraticForm _ (F.obj X)) (φ.dual X) m

/-- **The graded Leibniz rule for the Koszul differential**, on a product whose left factor is a
degree-one generator: `d (e ∧ x) = φ(e) · x - e ∧ d x`. Together with additivity and linearity
this determines the differential on the sections over `X`, since the exterior algebra of those
sections is generated by `F.obj X`; so the differential of Stacks tag 062K is the unique
derivation extending `φ`, as the source asserts.

The product is taken as a separate section `z` of degree `n + 1` whose value is the product,
rather than written out: the product of a degree-one and a degree-`n` section has degree
`1 + n`, and the two spellings of that integer are equal but not syntactically equal. -/
theorem exteriorAlgebraPieceVal_exteriorKoszulD_gen_mul (n : ℤ) (X : Cᵒᵖ) (m : F.obj X)
    (x : (exteriorAlgebraPiece n F).obj X) (z : (exteriorAlgebraPiece (n + 1) F).obj X)
    (hz : exteriorAlgebraPieceVal (n + 1) F X z =
      exteriorAlgebraPieceVal 1 F X (Hom.app (exteriorAlgebraGen F) X m) *
        exteriorAlgebraPieceVal n F X x) :
    exteriorAlgebraPieceVal n F X (Hom.app (exteriorKoszulD F φ n) X z) =
      φ.dual X m • exteriorAlgebraPieceVal n F X x -
        ExteriorAlgebra.ι ((O ⋙ forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat).obj X) m *
          Koszul.contraction (φ.dual X) (exteriorAlgebraPieceVal n F X x) := by
  rw [exteriorAlgebraPieceVal_exteriorKoszulD, hz, exteriorAlgebraPieceVal_gen]
  exact CliffordAlgebra.contractLeft_ι_mul (φ.dual X) m (exteriorAlgebraPieceVal n F X x)

/-- The Koszul differential into a negative degree is zero: the sectionwise exterior algebra has
no nonzero sections there. -/
theorem exteriorKoszulD_eq_zero_of_neg {n : ℤ} (hn : n < 0) : exteriorKoszulD F φ n = 0 :=
  hom_ext fun X => ModuleCat.hom_ext (LinearMap.ext fun _x =>
    exteriorAlgebraPiece_eq_zero_of_neg hn F X _)

end PresheafOfModules

end
